   "id": "yevamot.13a.11",
   "daf": "13a",
   "sentenceId": 10,
   "he": "וְכֹל שֶׁיְּכוֹלָה לְמָאֵן. וּתְמָאֵן הַשְׁתָּא, וְתִתְיַיבֵּם! לֵימָא מְסַיְּיעָא לֵיהּ לְרַבִּי אוֹשַׁעְיָא.",
   "en": "§ The mishna taught: «And» if «any» of these forbidden relatives was a minor «who could refuse» her husband, then even if she did not refuse him, her rival wife performs ḥalitza and does not enter into levirate marriage. The Gemara asks: «And let» the minor «perform refusal now,» thereby annulling the marriage retroactively after the death of her husband, «and let her» rival wife «enter into levirate marriage.» Since this option is not accepted, «let us say that it supports» the opinion «of Rabbi Oshaya.»"
  }
 ],
